    <h1>Projects</h1>
    <p class="intro">Systems I've designed and run on my own infrastructure. They exist because I wanted them, and they double as an honest signal: this is how I build when nobody is making me.</p>

    <div class="card">
      <h2 class="plain-title">Moneta</h2>
      <span class="card-context">Next.js 14 · Hono · SQLite + Drizzle · TanStack Query · local ML</span>
      <p>A self-hosted personal finance platform tracking six brokerage accounts with proper performance math — TWR, MWR, Sharpe, max drawdown — fed by SimpleFIN, Plaid, and broker exports. 7,000+ transactions, 3 years of history, running on a Mac at home. Local-only by design.</p>
      <a class="read-link" href="/work/moneta/">Read more →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h2 class="plain-title">SanthoshIAS</h2>
      <span class="card-context">Rust · Axum · priority-chain DataResolver · DuckDB · Redis</span>
      <p>A financial data gateway routing requests across six market data providers with automatic failover. One endpoint, one contract, six providers behind it. The same integration pattern used at institutional scale, pressure-tested at personal scale.</p>
      <a class="read-link" href="/work/santhoshias/">Read more →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h2 class="plain-title">FlowDeck</h2>
      <span class="card-context">Rust · flowengine crate · JSON filter DSL · WebSocket replay</span>
      <p>A self-hosted options-flow analytics platform that replaced a paid SaaS subscription. Live trade classification, z-score composite scoring, filters as JSON configuration. The full story is in the case study.</p>
      <a class="read-link" href="/work/flowdeck/">Read more →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h2 class="plain-title">APEX / AlphaEdge</h2>
      <span class="card-context">Python · FastAPI · React 18 · DuckDB · Bayesian expectancy · per-symbol state machines</span>
      <p>An options analytics and trading platform, now at v11. Five-layer safety architecture, Bayesian expectancy engine, market-character classification, and a postmortem-driven design process. Built like a production system because the consequences are real.</p>
      <a class="read-link" href="/work/apex/">Read more →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h2 class="plain-title">KidStream</h2>
      <span class="card-context">Pinchflat · Jellyfin · Swiftfin · Apple TV · NAS</span>
      <p>A curated, self-hosted media stack for children. Allowlisted content only, no algorithm, no ads, no tracking. The local-first philosophy applied to the toughest user base there is.</p>
      <a class="read-link" href="/work/kidstream/">Read more →</a>
    </div>

    <p class="body-text" style="margin-top: 32px;">All of it runs on a Terramaster NAS behind a Tailscale overlay network, in Docker, with local LLMs via Ollama where they earn their keep. The philosophy is consistent: local-first, self-hosted, zero unnecessary cloud dependency.</p>
